ipd: CPU RX throughput: GRO, NAPI weight 64, one CIDX MMIO read per batch

CPU RX (ASIC CPU port -> Linux) tops out around 400-430 Mb/s single stream
(iperf3 desktop -> switch, 65-69 retransmits) while the box is ~93% idle,
i.e. one core in softirq is the limit.  TX on the same path does 1.07 Gb/s.

Found by reading inno_rx_ring_poll()/inno_ring_poll() (not yet measured on
hardware, the switch was unreachable while this was written):

 * Every frame is handed up with netif_receive_skb() as CHECKSUM_NONE.
   There is no GRO, so each 1500-byte segment takes a full IP/TCP stack
   traversal and generates its own ACK work.  Use napi_gro_receive(); the
   skb is already header-linear (<=256 bytes) + page frag, which is what
   GRO wants.
 * The NAPI weight is 8.  Each poll invocation carries fixed costs (a
   REG32(SYNC_MODE) PCIe read, TX ring reap, the refill loop, napi_lock),
   so they were paid every 8 packets.  Use NAPI_POLL_WEIGHT (64).
 * The RX loop re-read RXQ_x_DESC_CIDX over PCIe MMIO after every packet.
   Re-read it only when the previously read batch has been consumed; the
   value comes from the same register, just less often.

Not changed here: per-descriptor alloc_page + dma_map_page refill with one
PIDX doorbell per page, single RX interrupt/NAPI context for all rings.

--- a/inno_enet.c
+++ b/inno_enet.c
@@ -1633,11 +1633,10 @@
 #endif
                 }
                 else {
-                    ret = netif_receive_skb(skb); /* Send the pkt out the xface */
-                    if (ret != NET_RX_SUCCESS){
-                        ndev->stats.rx_dropped++;
-                        ipd_debug("netif_receive_skb failed wth error %d\n",ret);
-                    }
+                    /* GRO: the ASIC gives no RX checksum/LRO, so without
+                     * this every MTU frame walks the stack on its own */
+                    (void) ret;
+                    napi_gro_receive(napi, skb);
                     ndev->stats.rx_packets++;
                     ndev->stats.rx_bytes += total_len;
                 }
@@ -1699,8 +1698,12 @@
             }
             need_release = 0;
         }
-        /* Update the posted_cidx */
-        posted_cidx = REG32(RXQ_x_DESC_CIDX(rx->num));
+        /* Update the posted_cidx.  This is a PCIe MMIO read (a full
+         * round trip); only pay for it once the batch already seen is
+         * consumed rather than once per packet. */
+        if (rx->cidx == posted_cidx) {
+            posted_cidx = REG32(RXQ_x_DESC_CIDX(rx->num));
+        }
     } /* while current cidx != posted cidx */
 
     rxq_cidx.flds.num_f = rx->cidx;
@@ -2007,9 +2010,9 @@
 
     /* Set up the NAPI polling */
 #if LINUX_VERSION_CODE < KERNEL_VERSION(6, 1, 0)
-    netif_napi_add(idev->ndev, &idev->napi, inno_ring_poll, 8);
+    netif_napi_add(idev->ndev, &idev->napi, inno_ring_poll, NAPI_POLL_WEIGHT);
 #else
-    netif_napi_add_weight(idev->ndev, &idev->napi, inno_ring_poll, 8);
+    netif_napi_add_weight(idev->ndev, &idev->napi, inno_ring_poll, NAPI_POLL_WEIGHT);
 #endif
 
     napi_enable(&idev->napi);
